<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκην-ίτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span> (in codd. sts. misspelt
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηνήτης</span>, which is accepted by
			<i><span class="en">
			Eust.
			70.29
		</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dweller in tents</i> or
				<i>booths</i>, of nomad tribes, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.2.1
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>one who keeps a stall,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				22.1672.15
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				171
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.2712.72
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Acraephia</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>a low fellow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				17.33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<i>in</i> or <i>belonging to a tent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κισσός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.36
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Eryc.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
